<title>FRANCE: French strike disrupts trains around Marseille.</title>
<headline>French strike disrupts trains around Marseille.</headline>
<dateline>MARSEILLE, France 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking ticket collectors disrupted railway traffic in the region of the French port city of Marseille on Thursday to press demands for the hiring of new staff, officials said.</p>
<p>State-owned railways SNCF said traffic had been slightly disrupted since Wednesday evening, adding that main lines and high-speed TGV trains were unaffected.</p>
<p>Some main-line trains stopped at more stations than usual to pick up stranded travellers.</p>
</text>
